@khorsheed/dsh-basic README · Make it yours：- **Remove a member**: disable/uninstall in Settings → Plugins, or `dsh plugin --profile <your profile> remove <package name>` — the rest keep working. The suite is a starting point, not a lock-in.
- **Add more**: any `@khorsheed/dsh-*` plugin installs the same way — copy the package name.
- **Update**: from Settings → Plugins, or `dsh plugin --profile <your profile> update` to pull the newest versions in range.

@khorsheed/dsh-basic README · 2. Installing a single plugin：- **Dialog**: Settings → Plugins → Add plugin, enter the package name (e.g. `@khorsheed/dsh-whalesong`), enable as prompted.
- **CLI**: `dsh plugin --profile <profile> add <package name>`; `remove` to uninstall, `update` to upgrade.

</details>
